# A lane that checks the turns laid out has to lay them out. testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime and testing=TestsEveryPosition write checks into each turn in the walk (CheckProof, Box, StrictEq, HasArrayStorage,
# GetArrayLength), a turn that holds them is not laid out, and so every check of the emitters on what a front has found was text that never ran. Under testing=EmittersAloneTestEveryPosition the walk writes nothing
# more: the same loops are laid out, in the same ways, as in an executable, and the checks stand in their turns.
# RUN: compile LoopsWhoseTurnsAreLaidOut LoopsLaidOutBehindBoundsOfMaskedKeys LoopsLaidOutForEachKindOfView KindsOfListsReadInFrontOfTurnsLaidOut KindsFoundInFrontOfTurnsHeldAgainstCells mechanisms=all
